WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.933
HIPAA training. Module 7. Privacy and security incidents and breaches.

2
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:13.767
An incident is anything that may have exposed patient information, or broken a rule.

3
00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.667
If you wonder whether it is an incident, report it.

4
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.633
An incident is reported by anyone, the same day.

5
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:29.700
A breach is decided by the client and ERS after an assessment, not by you.

6
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.967
The clock starts the day anyone in the workforce knows.

7
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:39.033
ERS tells the client right away.

8
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:43.800
Within 60 days, the client tells each affected person, in writing.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.033
Stop what you are doing with the information.

10
00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.533
Tell your lead and HR immediately.

11
00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:54.867
Describe what happened, without patient names.

12
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.600
Keep the evidence. Delete nothing.

13
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.400
Report right away.

14
00:01:00.733 --> 00:01:02.367
Write facts only.

15
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.600
Do not fix it quietly.

16
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:07.500
Do not delete or edit records.

17
00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.267
Stop.

18
00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.667
Do not share.

19
00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:12.200
Ask your lead.

20
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.333
Now read the module.
